WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:08.230
<v Narrator>It's 11:42 at night, and Contoso is paging its on-call technician.

2
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.010
<v Narrator>Most pages are a number to call back.

3
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:13.340
<v Narrator>This one arrives with the answers.

4
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.933
<v Narrator>Tenants call the maintenance line's Teams number.

5
00:00:23.013 --> 00:00:25.830
<v Narrator>Call Automation answers, and places each page.

6
00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:29.233
<v Narrator>Voice Live, with GPT Realtime, talks to both.

7
00:00:29.313 --> 00:00:32.860
<v Narrator>Your server decides who to wake, and writes the brief.

8
00:00:35.277 --> 00:00:37.464
<v Narrator>Here's where that page starts.

9
00:00:37.544 --> 00:00:42.017
<v Narrator>Wednesday, 11:42 at night, Alice Rivera calls the after-hours line.

10
00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:45.923
<v Agent>Contoso Property Management maintenance line.

11
00:00:46.003 --> 00:00:47.933
<v Agent>I'm an automated assistant.

12
00:00:48.013 --> 00:00:52.928
<v Agent>If anyone is in danger, or you smell gas or see fire, hang up and call 911 now.

13
00:00:53.008 --> 00:00:55.190
<v Agent>Otherwise, what's the problem?

14
00:00:56.519 --> 00:01:00.429
<v Alice>Water is pouring through my kitchen ceiling and it's spreading fast.

15
00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.963
<v Agent>Understood — an active leak.

16
00:01:03.043 --> 00:01:05.910
<v Agent>Is this about unit 4B at Maple Court?

17
00:01:07.264 --> 00:01:09.062
<v Narrator>The agent fills in fields.

18
00:01:09.142 --> 00:01:12.430
<v Narrator>The server's triage rules call an active leak urgent;

19
00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:14.774
<v Narrator>the model never picks a severity.

20
00:01:15.645 --> 00:01:21.455
<v Alice>Yes, 4B. You can go in — the spare key is in the lockbox by the back door.

21
00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:25.737
<v Agent>Is the number ending 0101 the best one to call you back on?

22
00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:29.063
<v Alice>Yes, that's my cell.

23
00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:31.744
<v Agent>I'm contacting the on-call technician now.

24
00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:34.101
<v Agent>You'll get a call back when they have it.

25
00:01:34.181 --> 00:01:37.226
<v Agent>If you can do so safely, shut off the nearest water valve

26
00:01:37.306 --> 00:01:39.230
<v Agent>while we contact the technician.

27
00:01:40.591 --> 00:01:42.240
<v Narrator>The rotation says Morgan.

28
00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:45.174
<v Narrator>The Teams card already has the unit, the problem

29
00:01:45.254 --> 00:01:47.611
<v Narrator>and the way in, and no phone numbers.

30
00:01:48.364 --> 00:01:49.797
<v Narrator>Listen for the brief.

31
00:01:49.877 --> 00:01:53.634
<v Narrator>The server writes it from those fields; the model only reads it.

32
00:01:54.492 --> 00:01:55.852
<v Morgan>Morgan Lee here.

33
00:01:56.169 --> 00:01:58.731
<v Agent>This is the Contoso Property Management pager,

34
00:01:58.811 --> 00:02:02.089
<v Agent>an automated assistant, with an urgent page for Morgan Lee.

35
00:02:02.475 --> 00:02:06.749
<v Agent>Urgent: active leak at Maple Court, unit 4B, reported 11:42 PM.

36
00:02:06.829 --> 00:02:12.207
<v Agent>Tenant said: Water is pouring through my kitchen ceiling and it's spreading fast.

37
00:02:12.287 --> 00:02:17.113
<v Agent>You may enter. Access: The spare key is in the lockbox by the back door.

38
00:02:17.193 --> 00:02:20.075
<v Agent>Press 1 or say 'I've got it' to accept.

39
00:02:21.388 --> 00:02:23.168
<v Morgan>I've got it — on my way.

40
00:02:23.518 --> 00:02:26.517
<v Agent>Thanks, Morgan. I'll tell the tenant you have it.

41
00:02:26.597 --> 00:02:29.298
<v Agent>The access details are on your Teams card.

42
00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:32.670
<v Agent>A technician has your request and will call you shortly.

43
00:02:34.709 --> 00:02:38.394
<v Narrator>Same night, at Pine Terrace, where Omar Diaz is on call.

44
00:02:38.474 --> 00:02:41.769
<v Narrator>Dee Nguyen's heat is out, and it's getting cold.

45
00:02:42.779 --> 00:02:47.411
<v Dee>The heat is out in unit 11 at Pine Terrace and it's 52 degrees in here.

46
00:02:47.491 --> 00:02:49.399
<v Dee>You can let yourself in.

47
00:02:49.733 --> 00:02:55.443
<v Agent>Understood — no heat. Is the number ending 0103 the best one to call you back on?

48
00:02:56.782 --> 00:03:01.622
<v Narrator>52 degrees is under the 55-degree no-heat line in config, so it's urgent.

49
00:03:02.403 --> 00:03:03.303
<v Dee>Yes.

50
00:03:03.405 --> 00:03:05.950
<v Agent>I'm contacting the on-call technician now.

51
00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:08.522
<v Agent>You'll get a call back when they have it.

52
00:03:08.603 --> 00:03:13.065
<v Agent>Please avoid unsafe heating sources such as ovens or outdoor heaters indoors.

53
00:03:15.973 --> 00:03:20.555
<v Narrator>No answer. The server's timer allows two tries per level, three minutes apart.

54
00:03:20.635 --> 00:03:22.533
<v Narrator>The demo clock skips ahead.

55
00:03:28.232 --> 00:03:29.132
<v Priya>I've got it.

56
00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:31.956
<v Agent>Thanks, Priya. I'll tell the tenant you have it.

57
00:03:32.036 --> 00:03:34.442
<v Agent>The access details are on your Teams card.

58
00:03:34.792 --> 00:03:37.822
<v Agent>A technician has your request and will call you shortly.

59
00:03:39.165 --> 00:03:41.119
<v Narrator>Two misses, then the secondary.

60
00:03:41.199 --> 00:03:44.955
<v Narrator>Priya's acknowledgement canceled the 20-minute operations alert.

61
00:03:47.044 --> 00:03:48.005
<v Narrator>Thursday night.

62
00:03:48.085 --> 00:03:49.862
<v Narrator>Priya swapped shifts with Morgan,

63
00:03:49.942 --> 00:03:53.474
<v Narrator>so when Ben Carter is locked out at Maple Court, the page goes to her.

64
00:03:54.439 --> 00:03:57.669
<v Agent>Contoso maintenance has an urgent page for you.

65
00:03:57.749 --> 00:04:01.359
<v Agent>Please call the maintenance line. Reference 2 4 6 0.

66
00:04:02.701 --> 00:04:05.280
<v Narrator>Anyone near the phone could hear that.

67
00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:10.041
<v Narrator>So the server keeps the building, the unit and the problem off voicemail.

68
00:04:12.102 --> 00:04:16.316
<v Narrator>Saturday, 10:15 at night, and Grace Kim's bedroom heat is out.

69
00:04:16.396 --> 00:04:18.972
<v Narrator>Is that worth waking a technician?

70
00:04:19.948 --> 00:04:24.668
<v Grace>The heat is out in my bedroom, but it's about 64 degrees inside.

71
00:04:24.963 --> 00:04:28.703
<v Agent>Understood — no heat. Is this about unit 7 at Pine Terrace?

72
00:04:30.033 --> 00:04:34.312
<v Narrator>64 degrees is above the 55-degree line, so the server calls it routine.

73
00:04:34.392 --> 00:04:36.433
<v Narrator>The model doesn't get a vote.

74
00:04:37.314 --> 00:04:41.594
<v Grace>Yes, unit 7. You can go in, I'm home all weekend.

75
00:04:41.892 --> 00:04:46.122
<v Agent>Is the number ending 0104 the best one to call you back on?

76
00:04:47.465 --> 00:04:48.365
<v Grace>Yes.

77
00:04:48.483 --> 00:04:51.673
<v Agent>This isn't urgent enough to page the on-call technician,

78
00:04:51.753 --> 00:04:54.279
<v Agent>so I've logged a work order for the office.

79
00:04:54.359 --> 00:04:56.374
<v Agent>They'll follow up Monday morning.

80
00:04:56.454 --> 00:04:58.928
<v Agent>If it drops to 55 degrees or below inside,

81
00:04:59.008 --> 00:05:02.023
<v Agent>call us back and we'll page the on-call technician.

82
00:05:03.377 --> 00:05:06.977
<v Narrator>Nobody woke up, and the work order keeps every detail.

83
00:05:08.627 --> 00:05:12.877
<v Narrator>The model listens, fills in fields, and reads the brief it's handed.

84
00:05:12.957 --> 00:05:15.577
<v Narrator>It never picks a severity or a person.

85
00:05:16.027 --> 00:05:18.908
<v Narrator>Your server classifies, picks the on-call chain,

86
00:05:18.988 --> 00:05:21.367
<v Narrator>writes the brief and runs the timers.

87
00:05:23.567 --> 00:05:26.586
<v Narrator>Most changes are configuration: triage rules,

88
00:05:26.666 --> 00:05:30.057
<v Narrator>rotations and swaps, escalation timers, buildings.

89
00:05:30.507 --> 00:05:35.147
<v Narrator>The spec and this demo script give your coding agent the context for the rest.

90
00:05:37.747 --> 00:05:39.295
<v Narrator>Contextual on-call pager.

91
00:05:39.375 --> 00:05:43.617
<v Narrator>Run it in simulation in two minutes, then connect it to your own Teams number.
